# ============================================================
#  eplan-mcp  —  WHITELIST-ONLY .gitignore
#
#  Philosophy: ignore EVERYTHING by default, then re-allow only
#  the files and folders reviewed and approved as public. A
#  whitelist fails closed: anything not explicitly allowed below
#  is never tracked. There is therefore no need to enumerate
#  individual private files -- enumerating them would itself leak
#  information about what is intentionally kept out of the repo.
#
#  To publish a new file, add an explicit "!" allow rule for it.
#  When in doubt, leave it out.
# ============================================================

# --- Block everything first ---
*

# --- Allow directories to be traversed so nested allows can match ---
!*/

# --- Standard OSS metadata (repo root) ---
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!VERSION
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!SECURITY.md
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!package.ps1

# --- Public framework sources ---
!src/**/*.py
!src/config.template.json

# --- Reference add-in (stub) ---
!addin/*.cs
!addin/build.ps1
!addin/README.md

# --- Public user-facing documentation ---
!docs/*.md

# --- Examples ---
!examples/**/*.py
!examples/**/*.md
!examples/**/*.json

# ============================================================
#  Generic safety net (defense-in-depth).
#
#  The whitelist above already fails closed; the patterns below
#  add belt-and-braces coverage against common artifact TYPES.
#  They name file types only, never specific assets, so this
#  section carries no information about what is kept private.
# ============================================================

# --- Compiled binaries / debug symbols ---
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.so
*.dylib

# --- Local configuration and secrets ---
config.json
config.local.json
secrets.json
.env
*.key
*.pem

# --- Runtime scratch / lock files ---
*.flag
*.log

# --- Backups and archives ---
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar.gz

# --- Python build, cache, and environment ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/

# --- IDE / editor ---
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
